tions to stabilize the generation process. Fig. 7 : Visualization of the semantic hierarchy in a U-Net-based diffusion model. Columns show three denoising timesteps ( t = 1000,100 , 10 t=1000,100,10 from left to right), and rows exhibit the noisy inputs and feature heatmaps from 3 representative ResBlocks. Due to the symmetry of the U-Net, we restrict the visualization to the first half of the network. Early ResBlocks (e.g., ResBlock5) mainly respond to local textures and edges, while deeper blocks (ResBlock14, ResBlock17) emphasize object parts and global scene layout. This phenomenon motivates our design of hierarchical modulation, whereby different ResBlocks are conditioned by coarse- and fine-grained semantics.
